 No observed target tensor or physical anisotropy parameter is measured here. In particular, full-tensor nonlinear quantities remain undefined in sectors where the target is unobserved or the required denominators are absent. A frequency axis supplies no depth information. The finite response results do not infer a local or global tilt, identify a Bianchi family, or validate a native cosmological solver. Their use is to specify which additional response directions or physically justified foreground restrictions an observational analysis must supply.
 
+\section*{Data availability}
+The finite response matrices and complete signed coordinate order are included with the source archive in \texttt{data/R31\_RESULT.json}; \texttt{data/RESULT.json} contains the bounded-moment sufficient statistics. The accompanying \texttt{data/SPECTRAL\_ONLY\_CONTRACT.md} specifies the released response products, retained nodes and normalization used in Eqs.~\eqref{eq:response}--\eqref{eq:spectra}. The runnable \texttt{consumer.py} reads the retained numerical values, \texttt{publication.py} generates the tables and figures, and \texttt{reproduce.py} rebuilds the complete paper. Original source identities and local copies are bound in \texttt{SOURCE\_BINDINGS.json}.
